    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task was to expose a human-readable `telephoneDisplay` field on the owner API while keeping the raw `telephone` in E.164 form. The project generates `OwnerDto` from `openapi.yml` and maps it from the `Owner` entity's transient getters via MapStruct, so I made two matching changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct auto-maps it by name (the same pattern as `displayName`, `initials`, `locality`, etc.).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getTelephoneDisplay()` deriving the display string from the stored E.164 value: it splits off the country code (`+1` NANP = 1 digit, otherwise 2 digits, matching the recognized `+61`/`+1` forms this app normalizes to), then re-joins as `country code` + space + national digits grouped in threes. It returns the raw value unchanged when the telephone is absent or not a `+`-prefixed digit run (so non-normalized seed data doesn't break).\n\nFor the test's stored `+61412345678` this yields `+61 412 345 678`, while `$.telephone` stays `+61412345678`.\n\n- Target test `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay`: **passes**.\n- Full `mvn test`: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1 test, 0 failures/errors (the only concrete test class; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper).",
